d_at`\n  - preserves row counts and order references\n  - removes the sidecar table/triggers\n- `postcheck.sql`\n  - checks user/order row counts\n  - checks dirty-user order preservation\n  - checks exact cleaned emails\n  - checks `created_at` preservation\n  - checks `email` non-null + unique behavior\n  - checks `status` non-null/default definition\n- `migration_report.md`\n  - summarizes strategy, cleanup, idempotency, rollback behavior, postcheck usage\n\nVerification\n- Applied schema, ran migration once, ran postcheck: all checks returned `ok`.\n- Ran migration a second time, ran postcheck again: all checks returned `ok`.\n- Verified rerun preserves status changes:\n  - after `update users set status='disabled' where id='u2';`\n  - reran migration\n  - query returned `u2|disabled`\n- Ran rollback:\n  - `pragma table_info(users)` returned only:\n    - `id`\n    - `email`\n    - `name`\n    - `created_at`\n  - row counts after rollback: `6` users, `4` orders\n  - remaining tables after rollback: `orders,users`\n  - remaining triggers after rollback: none\n\nCommands run\n- `sqlite3 --version`\n- `tmp=$(mktemp /tmp/sqlite-probe.XXXXXX.db) && sqlite3 \"$tmp\" \"create table t(a); alter table t add column if not exists b text; pragma table_info(t);\" && rm \"$tmp\"`\n- `tmpdir=$(mktemp -d /tmp/hb-migration.XXXXXX) && db=\"$tmpdir/test.db\" && sqlite3 \"$db\" \".read in/db/schema.sql\" && printf '\\n-- migrate once --\\n' && sqlite3 \"$db\" \".read in/db/migration.sql\" && sqlite3 \"$db\" \".read in/db/postcheck.sql\" && printf '\\n-- migrate twice --\\n' && sqlite3 \"$db\" \".read in/db/migration.sql\" && sqlite3 \"$db\" \".read in/db/postcheck.sql\" && printf '\\n-- rollback --\\n' && sqlite3 \"$db\" \".read in/db/rollback.sql\" && sqlite3 \"$db\" \"pragma table_info(users); select count(*) as users from users; select count(*) as orders from orders; select group_concat(name, ',') from (select name from sqlite_master where type='table' order by name); select group_concat(name, ',') from (select name from sqlite_master where type='trigger' order by name);\" && rm -rf \"$tmpdir\"`\n- `tmpdir=$(mktemp -d /tmp/hb-status.XXXXXX) && db=\"$tmpdir/test.db\" && sqlite3 \"$db\" \".read in/db/schema.sql\" && sqlite3 \"$db\" \".read in/db/migration.sql\" && sqlite3 \"$db\" \"update users set status='disabled' where id='u2';\" && sqlite3 \"$db\" \".read in/db/migration.sql\" && sqlite3 \"$db\" \"select id, status from users where id='u2';\" && rm -rf \"$tmpdir\"`\n- `git rev-parse HEAD`\n- `wc -l in/db/migration.sql in/db/preflight_report.md in/db/rollback.sql in/db/postcheck.sql in/db/migration_report.md`\n\nFinal HEAD SHA\n- `e8c5272a251a9309192401e5a0acb9de1c543476`\n\nAssumptions\n- None beyond standard SQLite behavior used by the verified `sqlite3` CLI run.\n\nUnresolved risks\n- None observed in the verified migration, rerun, status-preservation, and rollback paths.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_03c3c916e10de3f6016a888ec8179487d19a354b72a817754a\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":1062,"output":1792,"cacheRead":44032,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":46886,"reasoningTokens":721,"cost":{"input":0.0026550000000000002,"output":0.02688,"cacheRead":0.011007999999999999,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.040543}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1787334329788,"responseId":"resp_03c3c916e10de3f6016a888eba363487d18b5a798dd653d98f","duration":33410.034125000006,"ttft":1133.4090420000139},"toolResults":[]}
